@PhillipDefranco I am sort of floored that the feel good story is exactly what my mother helped coordinate for the Foster Grandparent Program, a program started by Nancy Reagan but federal funding cut off by President Bush Jr. 
My mother worked hard to place low income seniors with special needs, such as tutoring school children, holding babies who had no families or were in ICUs or  visiting those in adult group homes... They received a small stipend and transportation repayment and for every $1 spent, my mother proved it saved at least $3 in the long term, because it was a volunteering effort. 
The program is still around but most have shuttered as federal funding was cut in 2005.

@PhilipDeFranco
PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE bring back the good news minute you were doing. We NEED stories like the last one. I'm a retired public health nurse and I wept seeing those tiny bundles being loved on by that wonderful gentleman. 💖💖 The world feels like it's at a tipping point, no different than my mother described it when WWII started. Good news is needed now more than ever. Thanks
Jenn in Canada 🇨🇦
